WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.796
This is how an independent party starts. Not in Washington. In a
gymnasium in a county you have probably never heard of.

2
00:00:07.076 --> 00:00:12.913
Three short videos. Three people start it, fifty people write
it, and then it goes on the public record.

3
00:00:13.463 --> 00:00:16.100
Part one. Three people and a county.

4
00:00:16.650 --> 00:00:24.401
It starts with three people who live here. Not politicians. A
school bus driver, a nurse, and a man who runs a small sawmill.

5
00:00:24.681 --> 00:00:31.718
They sit on a porch and say the thing out loud. We want an
independent party for our county. Something that answers to us.

6
00:00:32.268 --> 00:00:36.506
A county is small enough that people can actually know each
other, and big enough to matter.

7
00:00:36.786 --> 00:00:42.539
The people who decide about your water, your timber, your roads
and your schools mostly live in the same county you do.

8
00:00:42.819 --> 00:00:47.456
So the first thing the three of them agree on is the name. The
Liberty County I P A.

9
00:00:48.006 --> 00:00:54.883
Then they do the hard part. They make a list of fifty people to
invite. Not fifty supporters. Fifty people who live here.

10
00:00:55.163 --> 00:01:05.238
So they walk the county to build it. Black families, white families, brown families. Jews, Muslims, Christians, Baptists,
Catholics.

11
00:01:05.518 --> 00:01:10.475
The business commission. The forestry service. The timber
companies, and the men who cut for them.

12
00:01:10.755 --> 00:01:17.471
Nonprofit groups. The handicapped veterans group. The people who
agree with them, and the people who flat out do not.

13
00:01:18.021 --> 00:01:26.259
Some doors close in their face. That is the point. If the room
only holds people who already agree, it is a club, not a county.

14
00:01:26.539 --> 00:01:33.818
The invitation says the same thing to everyone. Come help write
the context. Fifty seats. No speeches. One day.

15
00:01:34.368 --> 00:01:41.963
The veterans hall gets an invitation. So does the mill office, the churches, the mosque, the synagogue, the nonprofit desk, and
the forestry office.

16
00:01:42.243 --> 00:01:48.232
By the end of the month the list is full. Fifty people, and not
one of them was picked because they were safe.

17
00:01:48.782 --> 00:01:55.019
On a Saturday morning, fifty people walk into the high school
gymnasium and set up folding chairs in a single circle.

18
00:01:55.299 --> 00:02:01.936
No head table. No microphones. A stack of butcher paper, a box
of markers, and one question on the wall.

19
00:02:02.486 --> 00:02:11.762
The question is not what the county can do for us. It is how we want our lives to be, here, socially, economically, spiritually,
and in the woods and water around us.

20
00:02:12.042 --> 00:02:15.558
Everything the party does after that gets measured against this
one answer.

21
00:02:16.108 --> 00:02:23.466
That is video one. In video two, those fifty people sit in that circle and write down the future of Liberty County, five hundred
years out.

22
00:02:23.746 --> 00:02:28.382
In video three, that context goes on the public record at usaipa
dot org.
